id "answer-field-bcefd7d7-6332-5b93-9f2c-e15574d03741" :answer-field/id #uuid "bcefd7d7-6332-5b93-9f2c-e15574d03741" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c9023723-f6af-5dbc-9f3c-83dd8cbd448c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bab99505-cf3b-5584-bca4-4d0e0cbc9cd4" "answer-c9023723-f6af-5dbc-9f3c-83dd8cbd448c" "answer-61b25edc-b99e-5683-bc78-86b9980302d6" "answer-689ca3d8-8583-5b72-bea0-6f1b9b6117f6" "answer-f578f28e-933d-5e8f-878b-46984a7720a7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bab99505-cf3b-5584-bca4-4d0e0cbc9cd4" :answer/id #uuid "bab99505-cf3b-5584-bca4-4d0e0cbc9cd4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{Col}({A}^{-1})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c9023723-f6af-5dbc-9f3c-83dd8cbd448c" :answer/id #uuid "c9023723-f6af-5dbc-9f3c-83dd8cbd448c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{0\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-61b25edc-b99e-5683-bc78-86b9980302d6" :answer/id #uuid "61b25edc-b99e-5683-bc78-86b9980302d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-689ca3d8-8583-5b72-bea0-6f1b9b6117f6" :answer/id #uuid "689ca3d8-8583-5b72-bea0-6f1b9b6117f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{I}_{n\\times n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f578f28e-933d-5e8f-878b-46984a7720a7" :answer/id #uuid "f578f28e-933d-5e8f-878b-46984a7720a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}^{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a0f098cb-e297-54fe-a435-e8a16d43aa06" :question/id #uuid "a0f098cb-e297-54fe-a435-e8a16d43aa06" :question/math-academy-id "q-139977" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,{x}_{1}\\in R\\}?\n$$\n\nI. $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1$\n\nII. $A$ is invertible\n\nIII. $\\text{rank}(A)<4$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,{x}_{1}\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 4,$ or equivalently $\\text{rank}(A)<4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fa3f637a-f3b6-51d7-b9c4-70510038cd30"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fa3f637a-f3b6-51d7-b9c4-70510038cd30" :answer-field/id #uuid "fa3f637a-f3b6-51d7-b9c4-70510038cd30" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-538a5c83-1a7c-59fd-ac8b-ec6142e59eee" :answer-field/choices ["answer-78a8bbd0-591f-56da-86f2-7d40646b8958" "answer-538a5c83-1a7c-59fd-ac8b-ec6142e59eee" "answer-1df6b96c-ae37-5c0f-a45a-4777f6347ae1" "answer-32c9cac7-da71-5467-96f5-d4a01ec2f839" "answer-510c1195-aa8f-51b5-a011-ae59a01fa22b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78a8bbd0-591f-56da-86f2-7d40646b8958" :answer/id #uuid "78a8bbd0-591f-56da-86f2-7d40646b8958" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-538a5c83-1a7c-59fd-ac8b-ec6142e59eee" :answer/id #uuid "538a5c83-1a7c-59fd-ac8b-ec6142e59eee" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1df6b96c-ae37-5c0f-a45a-4777f6347ae1" :answer/id #uuid "1df6b96c-ae37-5c0f-a45a-4777f6347ae1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-32c9cac7-da71-5467-96f5-d4a01ec2f839" :answer/id #uuid "32c9cac7-da71-5467-96f5-d4a01ec2f839" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-510c1195-aa8f-51b5-a011-ae59a01fa22b" :answer/id #uuid "510c1195-aa8f-51b5-a011-ae59a01fa22b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9fbccd10-1c43-51a4-ad8b-36063e11427d" :question/id #uuid "9fbccd10-1c43-51a4-ad8b-36063e11427d" :question/math-academy-id "q-142367" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ is a solution of the equation $Ax=0?$\n\nI. $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0$\n\nII. $A$  is  invertible\n\nIII. $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4}$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is true. Since $v\\ne 0$ and $Av=0,$ \nthen $v\\in \\text{Null}(A)$ and, therefore, $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{4}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fec9750c-eaeb-571d-b465-6fa1ab05e88d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fec9750c-eaeb-571d-b465-6fa1ab05e88d" :answer-field/id #uuid "fec9750c-eaeb-571d-b465-6fa1ab05e88d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f1d58843-37c3-5988-8dac-72db97dcd1cf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-562361ed-d031-5fb2-9175-4571a3994648" "answer-f1d58843-37c3-5988-8dac-72db97dcd1cf" "answer-13e3d0a6-c269-5dde-bafd-a91861927c14" "answer-1848f756-51a0-5639-8084-5aa59abdaebf" "answer-8a7285e7-4a5d-5073-aa0f-ffd3853ddc65"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-562361ed-d031-5fb2-9175-4571a3994648" :answer/id #uuid "562361ed-d031-5fb2-9175-4571a3994648" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f1d58843-37c3-5988-8dac-72db97dcd1cf" :answer/id #uuid "f1d58843-37c3-5988-8dac-72db97dcd1cf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-13e3d0a6-c269-5dde-bafd-a91861927c14" :answer/id #uuid "13e3d0a6-c269-5dde-bafd-a91861927c14" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1848f756-51a0-5639-8084-5aa59abdaebf" :answer/id #uuid "1848f756-51a0-5639-8084-5aa59abdaebf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a7285e7-4a5d-5073-aa0f-ffd3853ddc65" :answer/id #uuid "8a7285e7-4a5d-5073-aa0f-ffd3853ddc65" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "lI only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186329820 :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\text{__________}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $A$ has no inverse\n\nII. $\\text{rank}(A)=n$\n\nIII. All columns of $A$ are pivot columns" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $A$ has no inverse.* $\\,✓$  \n\nIndeed,  a matrix $A$ is invertible if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\text{rank}(A)=n.$*$\\,\\times $\n\nSince our matrix is not invertible, according to the invertible matrix theorem, it must be $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne n.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.*  $\\,\\times $\n\nSince $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne n$, it must be $\\text{dim(Col}(A))<n,$ which means that not all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-251cfe7e-474d-59b2-8ccf-101401daf068" :question/id #uuid "251cfe7e-474d-59b2-8ccf-101401daf068" :question/math-academy-id "q-139978" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\text{__________}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $A$ has no inverse\n\nII. $\\text{Null}(A)$ has dimension zero\n\nIII. $A$ has less than $5$ pivot columns" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=5=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $A$ has no inverse.* $\\,✓$ \n\nIndeed, since $det(A)=0,$ the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $\\text{Null}(A)$ has dimension zero.* $\\,\\times $\n\nSince $A$ is not invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}$ which, in turn,  means that $\\text{Null}(A)$ must have a basis so the dimension must be greater than zero.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(A)=0,$ then $A$ has less than $5$ pivot columns.* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is not invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))\\ne 5,$ which means that $A$ has less than $5$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3b96ac14-685d-5526-ba37-eae6e8cc0fd7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3b96ac14-685d-5526-ba37-eae6e8cc0fd7" :answer-field/id #uuid "3b96ac14-685d-5526-ba37-eae6e8cc0fd7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-255616ee-ba3a-54d9-8723-c63b4106178b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-53cb8d5a-9998-5bf4-b2cf-fea2ed0d5668" "answer-255616ee-ba3a-54d9-8723-c63b4106178b" "answer-4db9632d-653a-5eaf-8753-6f387cc348fb" "answer-114ef65a-d282-56b9-8b1c-7327abc02824" "answer-0d6fe511-51db-512e-9712-3fce9ffdbf74"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-53cb8d5a-9998-5bf4-b2cf-fea2ed0d5668" :answer/id #uuid "53cb8d5a-9998-5bf4-b2cf-fea2ed0d5668" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-255616ee-ba3a-54d9-8723-c63b4106178b" :answer/id #uuid "255616ee-ba3a-54d9-8723-c63b4106178b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4db9632d-653a-5eaf-8753-6f387cc348fb" :answer/id #uuid "4db9632d-653a-5eaf-8753-6f387cc348fb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-114ef65a-d282-56b9-8b1c-7327abc02824" :answer/id #uuid "114ef65a-d282-56b9-8b1c-7327abc02824" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d6fe511-51db-512e-9712-3fce9ffdbf74" :answer/id #uuid "0d6fe511-51db-512e-9712-3fce9ffdbf74" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186125780 :tutorial/content "Suppose we are given an $n \\!\\times\\! n$ invertible matrix $A.$ Remember that if $A$ is invertible, then the equation $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}$ has only the trivial solution $\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}.$\n\nLet's extract all possible information from this fact using the vector spaces related to the matrix, namely, the *column space* and the *null space*.\n\n- The fact that the unique solution to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}$ is $\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}$ tells us that \n\n$$\n\\textrm{Null}(A)=\\{ \\mathbf{0} \\},\n$$\n\n or alternatively, \n\n$$\n\\textrm{dim(Null}(A)) = \\textrm{nullity}(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- Furthermore, if $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=0$ then $A$ has no *non-pivot* columns, or equivalently, all the columns of $A$ are *pivot columns*. So \n\n$$\n\\textrm{dim(Col}(A))=\\textrm{rank}(A)=n.\n$$\n\n- Finally, since $\\textrm{Col}(A)$ is a subspace of $\\mathbb{R}^n$ and its basis has $n$ linearly independent vectors, we can conclude that \n\n$$\n\\textrm{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^n.\n$$\n\nAll the results mentioned above can be summarized in the following theorem, called the **invertible matrix theorem**:\n\n*Let $A$ be an $n \\!\\times\\! n$ matrix. Then we have the following equivalence:*\n![](images/7e/7ef5d72a30dd7f79f6182c4d78d705a7771f9f90ff0bb50f6d539614cb1e5b4d.svg)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124685 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
